}
```

And a worker-counting helper. Where should it live? The existing spec file uses `page.addInitScript` inline for worker mocking. I'll add a helper in the spec file's describe block or in helpers.js. Since it's specific to these tests, I'll define it inside the describe block as a local function.

Fixture: twoAwayBoard() — free cells [K♠(51), Q♠(47)], foundations complete except ♠ missing Q,K (♠ A..J = pile(3).slice(0, 11)).

Wait — pile(3) = ranks 1..13 → ids r*4+3 for r=0..12: [3, 7, 11, ..., 51]. slice(0,11) = [3,...,43] (A..J). Then moves: Q♠(id 47)→home, K♠(51)→home.

Check auto-home interference: with auto-move ON, after Q♠ homes... K♠ canAutoHome? rank 13 > 2; opposite color = ♦/♥ both at 13 ≥ 12 ✓ → auto-homes immediately. So disable auto-move first via h.setAutoMove(page, false).

Also note: hint flow with worker — during computation the auto-solve toggle is disabled but that doesn't affect our clicks.

One important detail: when we click Q♠ and home slot — will interactions allow it? Click card in free cell selects; click home slot attempts move. attemptMove → gameState.attemptMove(state, {zone:"free",index:1}, "home", 3) — group length 1, canDropOnHome(♠ pile top J, Q) ✓ → ok. Auto-move disabled so no chain. 

Then board = B1: freeCells [51, null, null, null], foundations[3] = A..Q. Cache info: active true, remainingMoves 1.

Second hint: sync path → toast "ヒント: ♠Q → ホーム"... wait no — second time the remaining[0] is the K♠ move! After following Q♠→home, remaining = [K♠→home]. Toast: formatMove(K♠ move): id 51 → suit 3 ♠, rank (51>>2)+1 = 12+1 = 13 → "♠K" → "ヒント: ♠K → ホーム".

Let me now also double check the first hint's toast: solver returns moves[0] = Q♠→home (destIndex?). The solver uses destIndex = suit index? In view.showHint comment: "solverは destIndex をスート固定(0=♣,1=♦,2=♥,3=♠)で返す". So destIndex 3 for spades. Toast text "ヒント: ♠Q → ホーム". I'll assert `toContainText("ヒント")` mostly, and exact text for cache-hit hints where I know the move.

Worker counting mock:

```js
async function installCountingWorker(page) {
  await page.addInitScript(() => {
    window.__workerCount = 0;
    const NativeWorker = window.Worker;
    window.Worker = class CountingSolverWorker {
      constructor(url, opts) {
        window.__workerCount += 1;
        this._inner = new NativeWorker(url, opts);
        this.onmessage = null;
        this.onerror = null;
        this._inner.onmessage = (e) => this.onmessage?.(e);
        this._inner.onerror = (e) => this.onerror?.(e);
      }
      postMessage(m) {
        this._inner.postMessage(m);
      }
      terminate() {
        this._inner.terminate();
      }
    };
  });
}
```

And read count:
```js
const workerCount = (page) => page.evaluate(() => window.__workerCount);
```

Now the tests. Setup sequence per test:

```js
await installCountingWorker(page);
await h.openGame(page, 1);
await h.setAutoMove(page, false);
await h.setBoard(page, twoAwayBoard());
```

Wait — openGame injects helpers which calls setAnimationsEnabled(false). setBoard replaces board. Game #1 arbitrary since setBoard overrides.

Test 1: hint → follow → hint (cache hit, no re-search):

```js
test("ヒント→従う→ヒント: 2回目のヒントはキャッシュから即座に供給される", async ({ page }) => {
  await installCountingWorker(page);
  await h.openGame(page, 1);
  await h.setAutoMove(page, false);
  await h.setBoard(page, twoAwayBoard());

  // 1 回目のヒント: Worker で探索してキャッシュが作られる
  await page.click("#hint-btn");
  await expect(page.locator("#toast")).toContainText("ヒント: ♠Q → ホーム", { timeout: 10000 });
  expect(await workerCount(page)).toBe(1);
  expect(await h.solverCacheInfo(page)).toEqual({ active: true, remainingMoves: 2 });

