});
```

Hmm wait, one concern: toast visibility timing. First toast "ヒント: ♠Q → ホーム" appears. Then we click cards — does clicking clear the toast? Toast probably auto-dismisses. When second hint shows same-ish text... The second toast is "ヒント: ♠K → ホーム". `toContainText` on #toast — if the toast element retains old content until replaced... The first assertion waits for "♠Q"; second waits for "♠K" which only appears after second hint. OK distinct texts, no ambiguity.

But wait — there's a subtlety with the FIRST hint: the worker computes asynchronously. Between page.click("#hint-btn") and result, busy state disables stuff. The nearWinBoard test uses timeout 10000 for the toast. Fine.

Another subtlety — clicking Q♠ while hint highlight active: hint-source on Q♠. Clicking selects it; app.attemptMove clears hint highlight. Fine.

Test 2: deviate:

```js
test("ヒント→解から外す→ヒント: キャッシュは破棄され再探索される", async ({ page }) => {
