```

expect.poll polls until predicate true — robust. But also confirm hint actually displays eventually: wait for toast too (same text issue aside, it confirms completion). Use poll on workerCount primarily; then optionally check toast contains ヒント with generous timeout. Actually once workerCount===2 AND result arrives, toast shows. But the pre-existing toast may already contain that text... For determinism, I'll dismiss/ignore toast and just poll workerCount + verify solverCacheInfo becomes active again after the search completes:

After second search completes, cacheEntry rebuilt → getCacheInfo: { active: true, remainingMoves: 2 }. That's a solid completion signal without toast ambiguity:

```js
