  .toBe("true:2");
expect(await workerCount(page)).toBe(2);
```

Hmm, but there's a race: click hint → takeFromCache discards → worker starts (count=2) → result arrives → entry saved. Polling for active:true ensures full completion. 

Similarly for test 1's second hint, the toast text differs ("♠K"), so no ambiguity there. But let me double-check: could the SECOND hint's toast appear while first toast still displayed and toContainText match against stale "♠Q..."? No—we wait for "♠K" specifically. And workerCount stays 1 — asserted after toast appears. Good.

