I referenced `waitForCacheActive` but defined `waitForCacheRebuilt`. Let me generalize the helper to `waitForCacheActive` (poll until active:true with any remaining count) and use it where appropriate. For tests 2 and 5 I poll for "true:2" — those can keep using a stricter helper or just use waitForCacheActive + assert remainingMoves === 2 after. Let me restructure:

```js
/** ヒント要求の完了(キャッシュ再構築)を solverCacheInfo で待つ */
async function waitForCacheActive(page) {
  await expect
    .poll(async () => {
      const info = await h.solverCacheInfo(page);
      return info.active ? `true:${info.remainingMoves}` : "false";
    })
    .toMatch(/^true:/);
}
```

Then in tests 2 and 5: `await waitForCacheActive(page); expect(await h.solverCacheInfo(page)).toEqual({ active: true, remainingMoves: 2 });`

In the restart test: waitForCacheActive then capture. In auto-solve test, workerCount check suffices plus overlay visible.

